\description{
\code{stat_umap()} embeds the rows of the layer data in two dimensions with
Uniform Manifold Approximation and Projection (UMAP) and positions them at
the embedded coordinates. \code{geom_umap()} is a shortcut for
\code{stat_umap(geom = "point")}. Any other geom can render the embedding, e.g.
\code{stat_umap(geom = "text")} or \code{stat_umap(geom = "density_2d")}.
}
\details{
Feature columns are selected with \code{features}, using the same syntax as
\code{\link[dplyr:select]{dplyr::select()}}, from the layer data. Aesthetics such as \code{colour},
\code{shape} or \code{label} are carried along row by row; they never split the
computation into separate embeddings.
}
